    )),
    (477::bigint, jsonb_build_object(
      'queue_wait', 'Lunch and early happy hour are easy; weekend nights, major drag appearances and watch parties can stack an ID line along Halsted. Reserve tables for food or ticketed viewing events when offered. Bring physical 21+ ID and expect a cover on select nights.',
      'best_nights', 'Drag viewing parties and weekend dancing deliver the headline experience, while weekday trivia, karaoke or patio drinks feel more conversational. Arrive early for a table during a major broadcast. The best choice is the event you care about, not simply Saturday.',
      'crowd_mix', 'Gay men remain central, joined by drag fans, queer women, trans and nonbinary guests, allies, tourists and mixed birthday groups. Food and daytime hours broaden the ages; late parties skew younger. It is a high-visibility Northalsted institution rather than an intimate locals-only bar.',
      'dress_code', 'Casual through camera-ready both work: jeans, tees and trainers by day; sharper looks or fandom glamour for a viewing party. No blanket formal code is evident. Wear danceable shoes, bring valid ID and use layers if you plan to move between patio, dining room and floor.',
      'staff_inclusivity', 'Guests often praise upbeat bartenders, drag programming and a welcoming party atmosphere; busy-night reviews also cite slow service, crowding or door friction. The LGBTQ+ identity is longstanding and explicit. Reservations and clear checks make peak events smoother.',
      'venue_classification', 'active_long_running_northalsted_gay_tavern_restaurant_and_dance_venue_with_drag_viewing_parties_karaoke_trivia_patio_gay_male_core_broad_queer_ally_tourist_mix_and_positive_high_volume_consensus_with_peak_service_variability',
      'identity_note', 'Roscoe’s Tavern is an active gay restaurant, bar and event venue at 3356 N Halsted. It is not only a late-night club; daytime food and major drag viewing parties are core uses.',
